'' A VTABLE SLOT NAMES A FUNCTION THIS MODULE MAY NEVER SEE THE BODY OF.
''
'' 'declare virtual sub v( ) override' with no body anywhere put
'' @_ZN...1Q1VEv into Q's vtable, and clang answered "use of undefined value": taking
'' a function's address in LLVM needs it declared, and a pointer-table entry writes
'' the name straight out with no MirFunction behind it.
''
'' fbc ACCEPTS the same source -- an undefined virtual is a link-time question, not a
'' compile-time one -- so the object has to be producible. It is what
'' tests/vendor/fbc-tests/warnings/suffix-fb.bas writes, and the line that declines
'' does not mention a vtable.
''
'' void( ) is enough for the declaration: nothing calls through it. The vtable is
'' loaded and called indirectly with the call site's own signature, and a name this
'' module really does call has a MirFunction of its own and is not declared here.
'' TEST: cli
'' ARGS: --emit-ir tests/codegen/src/vtable-undefined-virtual.bas
'' EXPECT-EXIT: 0
'' EXPECT-OUT: declare void @"_ZN1Q1VEv"()
'' GOLDEN: expected/vtable-undefined-virtual.out
